  "proofs": {
    "P1_fusion": {
      "artefact": "ablation table",
      "verdict": "NOT fusion \u2014 'without nwp' scores highest",
      "head": "y_p5_w3",
      "test_positives": 4136,
      "honest_finding": "Leave-one-out shows ADVECTION is the dominant family (-0.040 CSI when removed) and that NWP as available HURTS at 0-6 h (+0.026 CSI when removed). Cause was measured, not guessed: NWP coverage starts at different dates (GFS 2021-03, ICON 2022-11, ECMWF 2024-02), so a column's missingness correlates with year and misleads on a fully-covered test year. Restricting to consistent-coverage columns recovers most of it (0.098 -> 0.116). The deeper reading is the project's own thesis: at 0-6 h, observation-based extrapolation beats global NWP \u2014 which is exactly the nowcast gap PRAVAAH exists to fill, and is consistent with RainFuse, where NWP at 6-72 h IS the signal and we beat it on Brier."
    },
