  "stated_limits": [
    "No ground radar. IMD's raw DWR volumes are gated; we log the public imagery every 10 minutes but do not decode it in v0. Radar is THE nowcasting instrument, so 0-6 h skill is bounded by its absence.",
    "ERA5-Land smooths convective extremes: 20.9 mm near Safdarjung on 28 Jun 2024 where the gauge recorded 228 mm. RainCast's thresholds are therefore ERA5-scale, and the charter's 15 mm/h head was dropped because it had only 63 test positives.",
    "IMD gridded is gauge-based and captures the extreme (150.7 mm) but is 0.25 deg \u2014 only 6 cells over the NCR box \u2014 so it is a daily areal truth, not a ward-scale one.",
    "Flood labels are 84 hand-curated points. Terrain alone does not explain them (top-quintile enrichment 0.94); OSM underpass features are the strongest available proxy for the missing variable, which is storm-sewer capacity.",
    "IMD's public CAP feed carried no Delhi-covering alert around the demo event, so lead-time-vs-CAP is not computable for it. That is reported as not-computable rather than substituted quietly."
  ],
